    {
      "id": 20651,
      "category": "researcher",
      "content": "While analyzing the Starbucks Korea mobile application, i noticed that it called an API at https://msr.istarbucks.co.kr:6443/appif/.\nIt was found that the application running under that directory was vulnerable to path traversal, allowing an attacker to read arbitrary files from the server. As a proof-of-concept I was able to retrieve system files, application source code, and logs.\n\nThank you @starbucks @agedsumatra @still for the good work.",
      "updated_at": "2020-03-10T21:58:04.612Z",
      "can_view?": true,
      "can_create?": false,
      "attachments": [],
